---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const effectiveDate = "September 16, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — SVGWire"
  description="SVGWire Privacy Policy. Read how SVGWire processes SVG files locally in your browser with zero server uploads, no user accounts, and no tracking."
  canonical="https://svgwire.com/privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[860px] px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body-sm text-mute">Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Privacy statement callout -->
    <div class="mb-12 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6">
      <h2 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Core Privacy Guarantee</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
        SVG files uploaded, pasted, or dropped into SVGWire are processed
        locally in your browser and are not uploaded to SVGWire servers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <div class="space-y-10 text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
      <!-- 1. Overview -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire ("we", "us", or "our") operates the web utility located at <a
            href="https://svgwire.com"
            class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">https://svgwire.com</a
          >. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you
          access and use our website and conversion tools.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          SVGWire is designed as a client-side web application. Vector
          processing, code generation, sprite compilation, and batch folder
          bundling take place within your local web browser environment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Information Processed -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          2. Information Processed
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire does not require user registration, account creation, or login
          credentials to access any feature. We do not intentionally request or
          collect personal identification information such as your name, email
          address, physical address, phone number, or payment details to use the
          converter.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          As described in Section 6, standard technical request information
          (such as your IP address and web browser user-agent) is processed by
          our infrastructure providers (Cloudflare and Google Fonts) when your
          browser requests web assets.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. SVG & File Processing -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          3. SVG & File Processing
        </h2>
        <p>
          When you paste raw SVG code, upload SVG files, or drop SVG directories
          into SVGWire:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Local Execution:</strong> All parsing, transformations, DOM manipulation,
            code generation (React, Vue 3, Svelte 5, React Native, and Tailwind CSS
            formats), sprite compilation, and ZIP archive creation are performed locally
            on your device using JavaScript and browser APIs (such as DOMParser and
            JSZip).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No File Uploads:</strong> SVG files and code input into the converter
            are not uploaded to or stored on SVGWire servers.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No Remote Database:</strong> We do not maintain a remote database
            or cloud storage of your SVG source files or generated component output.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Local & Session Storage -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          4. Local & Session Storage
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire does not set or use cookies for its own application
          functionality. Google Analytics may use first-party cookies for
          analytics measurement.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We utilize your web browser's storage APIs solely to preserve basic
          user interface preferences across your visits:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <code>localStorage.getItem('theme')</code>: Remembers your selected
            interface color theme (light or dark).
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>localStorage.getItem('svgwire-preview-bg')</code>: Remembers
            your chosen canvas preview background (light, dark, or transparent
            checkerboard).
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>sessionStorage.getItem('svgwire-framework')</code>: Preserves
            your active component framework selection when navigating between
            converter views during a browsing session.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This data remains stored locally on your device and can be cleared at
          any time through your web browser controls.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Analytics & Tracking -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          5. Analytics & Tracking
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire uses Google Analytics to understand general website usage,
          such as page views, traffic sources, and aggregate usage patterns.
          Google Analytics may collect information such as approximate location,
          browser and device information, and session statistics. Google
          Analytics may also use first-party cookies, such as the `_ga` cookie,
          to distinguish users and their sessions.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          SVGWire does not send SVG file contents, generated code, or the
          contents of files processed by the converter to Google Analytics. SVG
          processing remains local to your browser.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          SVGWire does not use advertising networks, session-recording tools, or
          social-media tracking pixels.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Third-Party Services & Hosting -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          6. Third-Party Services & Hosting
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our application relies on a minimal set of third-party infrastructure
          providers to deliver web pages and stylesheets:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Google Fonts:</strong> Web typography stylesheets are requested
            from Google Fonts (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code
              >fonts.gstatic.com</code
            >). Serving typography via Google Fonts involves standard technical
            network requests containing your IP address and user-agent string as
            governed by <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute"
              >Google's Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare Infrastructure:</strong> SVGWire's static web pages
            and assets are delivered via Cloudflare edge infrastructure. Cloudflare
            may process standard network request headers (including IP address and
            user-agent) at the network layer for CDN delivery, DDoS protection, security
            mitigation, and service stability as governed by <a
              href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute"
              >Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Your SVG files and code inputs are never transmitted to Google Fonts
          or Cloudflare as part of SVG conversion.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Data Retention -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          7. Data Retention
        </h2>
        <p>
          Because SVGWire does not maintain a remote database and does not
          upload user SVG files to SVGWire servers, we do not retain uploaded
          SVG files or converted code output on our servers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Security -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire is served exclusively over encrypted HTTPS connections.
          Client-side local browser processing serves as a key privacy and
          security design measure so your file contents remain on your device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Children's Privacy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          9. Children's Privacy
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire is a general-audience developer utility. We do not knowingly
          solicit or collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Changes to This Policy -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          10. Changes to This Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect updates
          in functionality or legal requirements. Any modifications will be
          posted directly on this page with an updated Effective Date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Contact Information -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          11. Contact Information
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or SVGWire, please
          contact us at:
        </p>
        <div
          class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-4 font-mono text-body-sm"
        >
          <p>
            Email: <a
              href="mailto:contact@svgwire.com"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">contact@svgwire.com</a
            >
          </p>
          <p>
            Website: <a
              href="https://svgwire.com"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">https://svgwire.com</a
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
